1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,389
What is love?

2
00:00:01,389 --> 00:00:04,201
Love is an act of bravery.

3
00:00:04,201 --> 00:00:06,256
What if she doesn't like me?

4
00:00:06,256 --> 00:00:07,678
What if she does?

5
00:00:07,678 --> 00:00:11,592
What if she's now ready
to open her heart to you?

6
00:00:11,592 --> 00:00:14,264
Ours was a love story like no other.

7
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:18,467
This story is not about
our "happily ever after".

8
00:00:18,467 --> 00:00:20,748
Take a leap of faith, Mr. Herrera.

9
00:00:20,748 --> 00:00:23,603
Maybe she's just waiting for you.

10
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,972
Hey, when will you wake up?

11
00:00:29,972 --> 00:00:31,277
I'm going to get up.

12
00:00:31,277 --> 00:00:33,957
Get up or you will get it from me
if I am late.

13
00:00:33,957 --> 00:00:40,218
Do you honestly think
that I dream of working for my dad?

14
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:58,585
Mrs. Herrera...

15
00:00:58,585 --> 00:01:00,988
Miss Marquez, where's my son?
And what happened?

16
00:01:00,988 --> 00:01:03,490
The doctors are already attending to him.

17
00:01:03,490 --> 00:01:05,325
Let's just wait for the doctor

18
00:01:05,325 --> 00:01:08,729
so he can explain to you
Dex's current situation.

19
00:01:08,729 --> 00:01:10,530
What happened?

20
00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:12,666
I am so sorry, Mrs. Herrera.

21
00:01:12,666 --> 00:01:14,060
I was watching him,

22
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:18,271
but I had to go to the office to double-check
if I had your numbers right,

23
00:01:18,271 --> 00:01:20,607
to make sure you will pick him up.

24
00:01:20,607 --> 00:01:25,478
Unfortunately, the guard didn't see
that he had gone out.

25
00:01:31,118 --> 00:01:33,120
Joyce.

26
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:34,755
What happened? Where's Dex?

27
00:01:34,755 --> 00:01:38,157
Where were you?
You're supposed to pick Dex up!

28
00:01:38,859 --> 00:01:40,694
Joyce...

29
00:01:40,694 --> 00:01:42,763
Answer me!

30
00:01:42,763 --> 00:01:44,398
Joyce, I couldn't leave soon...

31
00:01:44,398 --> 00:01:46,432
Where were you?

32
00:01:47,034 --> 00:01:49,870
- Where were you?
- Joyce, Joyce.

33
00:01:49,870 --> 00:01:52,338
- Joyce...
- Where were you?

34
00:01:57,210 --> 00:01:59,278
Where were you?

35
00:02:02,449 --> 00:02:04,217
Joyce, sorry.

36
00:02:06,153 --> 00:02:07,700
Sorry.

37
00:02:38,425 --> 00:02:40,493
My son.

38
00:02:46,827 --> 00:02:50,496
It's your fault
that your son had an accident.

39
00:02:51,998 --> 00:02:59,572
But being an irresponsible father
is your biggest fault.

40
00:03:01,942 --> 00:03:04,777
Dad, please, I'm begging you.

41
00:03:07,114 --> 00:03:10,884
Only you can help me and Dex.

42
00:03:10,884 --> 00:03:14,410
Dad, please, I'm begging you... Dad.

43
00:03:15,555 --> 00:03:17,167
Dad.

44
00:03:19,059 --> 00:03:21,594
Of course, I will help you.

45
00:03:22,295 --> 00:03:24,964
But I hope you learn your lesson.

46
00:03:27,167 --> 00:03:28,401
I told you many times over.

47
00:03:28,401 --> 00:03:32,838
Stop with your illusion of becoming a writer.

48
00:03:33,473 --> 00:03:36,008
You can't make money off of writing.

49
00:03:37,344 --> 00:03:44,016
You break your back working,
but you're neglecting your family.

50
00:03:46,686 --> 00:03:48,955
The problem with you is...

51
00:03:50,090 --> 00:03:54,594
that you think
I am the antagonist in your story.

52
00:03:54,594 --> 00:03:59,332
If you only listened to me
and continued working for me,

53
00:03:59,332 --> 00:04:02,301
you could have had a stable life.

54
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:07,310
You'd have money to support your family.

55
00:04:08,715 --> 00:04:12,541
You'd have time to care for your child.

56
00:04:30,630 --> 00:04:33,366
I've already deposited money to the hospital.

57
00:04:37,704 --> 00:04:42,008
And I have settled everything needed
for Dex's surgery.

58
00:04:45,879 --> 00:04:49,515
Keep that money for now,
so at least you have cash on you.

59
00:05:04,664 --> 00:05:06,432
Joyce...

60
00:05:12,906 --> 00:05:15,041
Joyce, I'm so sorry.

61
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:22,048
I'm sorry.

62
00:05:24,417 --> 00:05:26,952
This is all my fault.

63
00:05:44,104 --> 00:05:46,773
After the operation,

64
00:05:46,773 --> 00:05:50,677
Dex has to stay in the recovery room first.

65
00:05:50,677 --> 00:05:54,413
And then he'll get transferred
to a regular room.

66
00:05:55,609 --> 00:05:58,544
We can be by his side tomorrow.

67
00:06:04,724 --> 00:06:07,193
Go home for now.

68
00:06:08,361 --> 00:06:10,230
We'll just call you if there's an update.

69
00:06:10,230 --> 00:06:13,132
I'll stay here for now.

70
00:06:26,646 --> 00:06:28,447
Hon...

71
00:06:51,171 --> 00:06:52,939
<i>Don't you feel guilty?</i>

72
00:06:52,939 --> 00:06:57,009
<i>You have no time for your son and for Joyce.</i>

73
00:06:58,945 --> 00:07:01,881
<i>Is that the life you want for them?</i>

74
00:07:03,049 --> 00:07:09,021
<i>I promised your mother
that I will give you a good life.</i>

75
00:07:10,223 --> 00:07:12,792
<i>But what happened?</i>

76
00:07:12,792 --> 00:07:17,464
<i>You have turned out to be
my biggest disappointment.</i>

77
00:07:17,464 --> 00:07:20,766
<i>Your mother will never forgive me.</i>

78
00:07:29,609 --> 00:07:36,149
<i>Write everything you want to say.</i>

79
00:07:36,149 --> 00:07:41,254
<i>That way, I will know
what's inside your heart.</i>

80
00:07:41,254 --> 00:07:47,092
<i>Because I will make
all your wishes come true.</i>

81
00:08:34,707 --> 00:08:38,317
<i>Dear, Mom... It's me.</i>

82
00:08:38,317 --> 00:08:40,880
<i>I hope you're here.</i>

83
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:45,285
<i>I wish you were still alive
so that I could personally apologize.</i>

84
00:08:45,285 --> 00:08:48,555
<i>For I have become a disappointment.</i>

85
00:08:48,555 --> 00:08:53,459
<i>But I will feel shame if you can see me now.</i>

86
00:08:54,127 --> 00:08:57,097
<i>And I will feel ashamed to face you.</i>

87
00:08:57,097 --> 00:09:00,733
<i>I really tried, I promise.</i>

88
00:09:00,733 --> 00:09:02,735
<i>But I failed.</i>

89
00:09:04,270 --> 00:09:07,273
<i>And I failed miserably.</i>

90
00:09:12,812 --> 00:09:15,915
<i>My son is suffering because of me.</i>

91
00:09:15,915 --> 00:09:19,352
<i>Because of my shortcomings as a father.</i>

92
00:09:19,352 --> 00:09:23,656
<i>Worse, I hurt the person I love.</i>

93
00:09:23,656 --> 00:09:27,494
<i>I wasn't able to be a good husband to her.</i>

94
00:09:27,494 --> 00:09:32,932
<i>I wasn't able to give them a good life.</i>

95
00:09:32,932 --> 00:09:34,334
<i>Dad was right.</i>

96
00:09:34,334 --> 00:09:38,972
<i>I shouldn't have been a part of Joyce
and my son's life.</i>

97
00:09:38,972 --> 00:09:42,175
<i>I shouldn't have dragged them down
because of my weakness</i>

98
00:09:42,175 --> 00:09:46,012
<i>so that they wouldn't have suffered
because of my failures.</i>

99
00:09:46,012 --> 00:09:48,848
<i>If only I could undo the past...</i>

100
00:09:48,848 --> 00:09:51,518
<i>If only I could turn back time.</i>

101
00:09:51,518 --> 00:09:55,187
<i>I wish Joyce could be happy.</i>

102
00:09:56,489 --> 00:10:02,862
<i>If I could rewrite my story,
I wouldn't have followed her.</i>

103
00:10:02,862 --> 00:10:06,399
<i>I shouldn't have come into her life.</i>

104
00:10:06,399 --> 00:10:10,002
<i>I shouldn't have involved other people.</i>

105
00:10:21,881 --> 00:10:24,369
<i>Take a leap of faith.</i>

106
00:10:53,780 --> 00:10:55,547
Where am I?

107
00:10:57,584 --> 00:10:59,385
Good morning, Sir.

108
00:11:01,187 --> 00:11:03,075
Are you ready for today?

109
00:11:11,070 --> 00:11:13,749
Where am I? What am I doing here?

110
00:11:13,749 --> 00:11:16,358
Engineer William Herrera.

111
00:11:16,358 --> 00:11:17,913
I had a hunch you went drinking last night

112
00:11:17,913 --> 00:11:21,882
and I knew where to find you.

113
00:11:21,882 --> 00:11:27,106
Well, also last night,
you were with your girlfriend.

114
00:11:27,106 --> 00:11:29,455
She left early today.

115
00:11:29,455 --> 00:11:33,235
So I'm assuming you were

116
00:11:33,235 --> 00:11:36,697
basically doing boyfriend-girlfriend stuff.

117
00:11:36,697 --> 00:11:38,224
What did you say?

118
00:11:38,224 --> 00:11:40,259
Engineer William Herrera?

119
00:11:40,259 --> 00:11:42,794
What are you saying? And, girlfriend?

120
00:11:42,794 --> 00:11:45,266
Hey, I'm already married!

121
00:11:47,865 --> 00:11:49,141
And...

122
00:11:50,034 --> 00:11:52,094
why am I naked?

123
00:11:52,922 --> 00:11:54,372
What did you do to me?

124
00:11:54,372 --> 00:11:55,947
What did you do to me?

125
00:11:55,947 --> 00:11:58,277
Excuse me, Sir!

126
00:11:58,277 --> 00:12:02,180
Are you insinuating
that I did something unpleasant to you?

127
00:12:03,315 --> 00:12:04,590
Please!

128
00:12:04,590 --> 00:12:08,192
I've been your executive assistant for years!

129
00:12:08,192 --> 00:12:10,854
I've always been professional.

130
00:12:10,854 --> 00:12:13,423
Plus, knowing you,

131
00:12:13,423 --> 00:12:16,627
you will never allow
relationships between employees.

132
00:12:16,627 --> 00:12:20,719
Not to mention,
you like sleeping without a shirt on.

133
00:12:21,965 --> 00:12:23,667
Did my dad order you to do this?

134
00:12:23,667 --> 00:12:26,205
Tell me, is this a prank?

135
00:12:26,205 --> 00:12:29,873
Sir, you're more of a prankster than me.

136
00:12:29,873 --> 00:12:33,911
So I suggest you drop the innocent act.

137
00:12:33,911 --> 00:12:38,581
If you don't,
you'll be late for your first meeting.

138
00:12:39,918 --> 00:12:41,586
Dex!

139
00:12:42,321 --> 00:12:44,155
Dex.

140
00:12:49,952 --> 00:12:51,683
Sir!

141
00:12:53,129 --> 00:12:54,573
Sir!

142
00:12:54,573 --> 00:12:56,542
Taxi!

143
00:12:58,737 --> 00:12:59,802
Sir!

144
00:12:59,802 --> 00:13:01,568
- Boss, to City General.
- Sir, where are you going?

145
00:13:01,568 --> 00:13:02,985
- Sir, wait!
- Let's go.

146
00:13:02,985 --> 00:13:04,309
Sir!

147
00:13:07,105 --> 00:13:09,324
What's going on with him?

148
00:13:14,027 --> 00:13:15,957
Are you okay, sir?

149
00:13:22,393 --> 00:13:26,555
Mister, do you have a phone?

150
00:13:28,241 --> 00:13:31,602
Here it is, sir. Do you need to borrow it?

151
00:13:31,602 --> 00:13:33,336
Thank you.

152
00:13:38,317 --> 00:13:40,521
<i>Sorry, the subscriber cannot be reached.</i>

153
00:13:40,521 --> 00:13:42,113
<i>Please try again later.</i>

154
00:13:44,416 --> 00:13:46,852
<i>Sorry, the subscriber cannot be reached.</i>

155
00:13:46,852 --> 00:13:49,107
No.

156
00:13:49,107 --> 00:13:51,322
I can't contact her.

157
00:13:53,492 --> 00:13:56,458
Seems like you had a long night, sir.

158
00:13:56,458 --> 00:13:59,495
It's even worse.

159
00:13:59,495 --> 00:14:01,670
I don't remember anything.

160
00:14:03,375 --> 00:14:07,976
So don't party too much, sir.

161
00:14:07,976 --> 00:14:11,879
You can be forgetful
when you're having too much fun.

162
00:14:14,487 --> 00:14:16,780
Actually...

163
00:14:16,780 --> 00:14:20,149
Mister, I'm going to ask you a favor.

164
00:14:22,786 --> 00:14:24,880
I don't have my wallet with me.

165
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:29,493
But don't worry.
I'll pay you once I see my wife.

166
00:14:29,493 --> 00:14:30,794
She's in the hospital.

167
00:14:30,794 --> 00:14:33,196
She's looking after our son.

168
00:14:35,355 --> 00:14:37,234
Mister, please trust me.

169
00:14:37,234 --> 00:14:38,902
I'm not lying to you.

170
00:14:38,902 --> 00:14:41,104
I really do not know what happened.

171
00:14:41,104 --> 00:14:42,606
I can't remember anything.

172
00:14:42,606 --> 00:14:47,037
The problem is I don't recall anything.

173
00:14:47,037 --> 00:14:49,688
The last memory I have is...

174
00:14:49,688 --> 00:14:50,634
<i>Dad was right.</i>

175
00:14:50,634 --> 00:14:54,801
<i>I shouldn't have been
part of Joyce's and my son's life.</i>

176
00:14:54,801 --> 00:14:57,554
<i>If only I could erase the past...</i>

177
00:14:57,554 --> 00:15:00,891
<i>If only I could turn back the time.</i>

178
00:15:00,891 --> 00:15:02,696
Who are you?

179
00:15:02,696 --> 00:15:04,915
My last memory is...

180
00:15:04,915 --> 00:15:07,030
I was in the house.

181
00:15:07,030 --> 00:15:11,001
I can't remember
how I ended up in that building.

182
00:15:24,857 --> 00:15:26,149
Ma'am.

183
00:15:26,149 --> 00:15:28,852
- Yes, sir?
- How is my son's surgery?

184
00:15:28,852 --> 00:15:30,854
Is he already transferred to a regular room?

185
00:15:30,854 --> 00:15:32,929
What is your son's name?

186
00:15:34,558 --> 00:15:35,892
Dexter Herrera.

187
00:15:35,892 --> 00:15:37,632
Let me check, sir.

188
00:15:49,272 --> 00:15:51,508
What's his name again?

189
00:15:51,508 --> 00:15:53,744
Dexter Herrera. I'm his father.

190
00:15:53,744 --> 00:15:56,479
My name is William Herrera.

191
00:15:57,347 --> 00:16:00,583
I'm sorry, sir,
but your son's name is not in our records.

192
00:16:00,583 --> 00:16:02,586
What are you saying?

193
00:16:02,586 --> 00:16:06,589
Ma'am, can you please check again?
I'm sure you're mistaken.

194
00:16:09,326 --> 00:16:10,627
What's the problem?

195
00:16:10,627 --> 00:16:13,196
His son's name is not in our records.

196
00:16:13,196 --> 00:16:14,608
What do you mean there's no record?

197
00:16:14,608 --> 00:16:16,633
- He's really not here.
- I can't be wrong.

198
00:16:16,633 --> 00:16:18,034
We brought our son here!

199
00:16:18,034 --> 00:16:21,204
He had surgery
because of his injuries, remember?

200
00:16:21,204 --> 00:16:23,039
Are you joking?

201
00:16:23,039 --> 00:16:24,274
You're not funny!

202
00:16:24,274 --> 00:16:26,843
- Sir, he's really not here.
- Sir, you need to calm down.

203
00:16:26,843 --> 00:16:27,911
Calm down?

204
00:16:27,911 --> 00:16:30,887
You're telling me my son's not here.
How can I calm down?

205
00:16:30,887 --> 00:16:32,191
He's really not here.

206
00:16:32,191 --> 00:16:34,200
No! Joyce!

207
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:35,585
- Joyce!
- Sir, calm down!

208
00:16:35,585 --> 00:16:38,856
- Calm down my foot!
- Sir, your son's name is not here!

209
00:16:38,856 --> 00:16:39,888
Joyce!

210
00:16:39,888 --> 00:16:41,097
Sir!

211
00:16:41,097 --> 00:16:43,035
- Where are you?
- Sir!

212
00:16:43,035 --> 00:16:44,239
- Sir!
- Dex!

213
00:16:44,239 --> 00:16:46,396
- Sir.
- Sir, he's really not here!

214
00:16:46,396 --> 00:16:48,731
- Dex!
- Sir!

215
00:16:50,714 --> 00:16:52,803
Where's my son?

216
00:16:52,803 --> 00:16:55,071
Did you transfer him to another room?
Or has he been discharged?

217
00:16:55,071 --> 00:16:57,374
- He's not here.
- Tell me!

218
00:16:57,374 --> 00:16:59,409
Explain it to me! Where's my son?

219
00:16:59,409 --> 00:17:01,711
He's really not here.

220
00:17:04,412 --> 00:17:06,480
Where's my son?

221
00:17:12,331 --> 00:17:14,050
Are you okay, sir?

222
00:17:14,050 --> 00:17:17,327
How did my son suddenly disappear
from that hospital?

223
00:17:17,327 --> 00:17:19,505
Maybe we went to the wrong hospital.

224
00:17:19,505 --> 00:17:23,141
I know which hospital I left my son at.

225
00:17:28,271 --> 00:17:31,132
Sorry, Mister.

226
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:32,067
Maybe it's better

227
00:17:32,067 --> 00:17:36,167
if you'll bring me
to our house in Sto. Cristo instead.

228
00:17:36,167 --> 00:17:37,701
Maybe they already went home.

229
00:17:37,701 --> 00:17:40,733
At least I can finally pay you.

230
00:17:40,734 --> 00:17:43,493
Okay, sir. No problem.

231
00:17:51,210 --> 00:17:52,295
You can drop me off here.

232
00:17:52,295 --> 00:17:53,896
Okay.

233
00:17:55,273 --> 00:17:56,960
Mister, please, wait for me.

234
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:59,142
- I'll get some money.
- Okay, sir.

235
00:17:59,142 --> 00:18:00,671
Wait a second.

236
00:18:34,447 --> 00:18:38,250
Hon, I'm glad
Dex got discharged from the hospital.

237
00:18:44,414 --> 00:18:46,358
Hon.

238
00:18:46,358 --> 00:18:48,052
Hey!

239
00:18:48,052 --> 00:18:50,395
Why are you hugging my wife?

240
00:18:51,955 --> 00:18:55,125
Who are you? How did you get in here?

241
00:18:55,125 --> 00:18:57,160
What do you mean who am I?

242
00:18:57,160 --> 00:19:00,596
Who are you? Why are you in our house?

243
00:19:01,793 --> 00:19:05,501
Hey, hey! Don't come near me!

244
00:19:06,369 --> 00:19:08,571
- Come here, you pervert!
- Pervert?

245
00:19:08,571 --> 00:19:10,449
- I'm not a pervert!
- Come here, you pervert!

246
00:19:10,449 --> 00:19:12,717
What are you talking about?
I'm not a pervert!

247
00:19:12,717 --> 00:19:15,444
Come here! Come here!

248
00:19:17,213 --> 00:19:19,049
Here's a snow cabbage!

249
00:19:19,049 --> 00:19:21,350
Come here, pervert!

250
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:25,403
Wait! Let's talk it out.

251
00:19:25,403 --> 00:19:27,071
Let's talk it out.

252
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:31,828
- Mister!
- Hey!

253
00:19:31,828 --> 00:19:33,410
Come back here!

254
00:19:33,410 --> 00:19:35,107
Mister, start the car!

255
00:19:35,107 --> 00:19:37,137
- Hurry up!
- Hey, hey, mister!

256
00:19:37,137 --> 00:19:41,137
Hey! Mister, why did you leave me?

257
00:19:41,137 --> 00:19:42,639
Come here!

258
00:19:42,639 --> 00:19:44,974
I'll kill you!

259
00:19:48,954 --> 00:19:50,563
Hey, hey!

260
00:19:50,563 --> 00:19:52,260
- That's a pervert!
- Wait, wait.

261
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:53,416
I'm not a pervert!

262
00:19:53,416 --> 00:19:55,760
- Boss, boss... wait, wait!
- Stop him!

263
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:58,021
Wait, boss. Let's talk it out.

264
00:19:58,021 --> 00:20:00,056
- You're a pervert!
- I'm not a pervert!

265
00:20:00,056 --> 00:20:01,458
That's our house!

266
00:20:01,458 --> 00:20:03,860
- Why are you in our house?
- Beat him up!

267
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:06,429
Where's Joyce? Where's Dex? What's going on?

268
00:20:06,429 --> 00:20:08,687
- Pervert!
- Hey!

269
00:20:51,383 --> 00:20:54,548
You're lucky the village cops passed by

270
00:20:54,548 --> 00:20:57,584
and stopped those men from killing you.

271
00:20:57,584 --> 00:21:01,422
We have no choice but to
file a case against you.

272
00:21:01,422 --> 00:21:03,951
Your case is no joke.

273
00:21:03,951 --> 00:21:07,569
You entered someone else's house
and harassed that thug's wife.

274
00:21:07,569 --> 00:21:09,654
Chief, that's not true!

275
00:21:09,654 --> 00:21:14,366
You don't understand. That's our house!

276
00:21:14,366 --> 00:21:16,169
Looks like you are under
the influence of alcohol.

277
00:21:16,169 --> 00:21:17,896
What did you take?

278
00:21:17,896 --> 00:21:19,966
What are you saying?

279
00:21:19,966 --> 00:21:23,279
Maybe you should sober up first.

280
00:21:23,279 --> 00:21:27,114
Donaire, bring him in until he sobers up.

281
00:21:27,114 --> 00:21:28,782
Wait, wait, Sir! Sir...

282
00:21:28,782 --> 00:21:30,184
- Bring him in.
- Sir, Sir!

283
00:21:30,184 --> 00:21:31,985
I didn't do anything wrong!

284
00:21:31,985 --> 00:21:33,925
- Come on.
- Sir, Sir! Where are you bringing me?

285
00:21:33,925 --> 00:21:36,528
Hey, hey, hey!

286
00:21:36,528 --> 00:21:39,155
- Hey, Sir! Sir, I don't want to go to jail.
- Hurry up.

287
00:21:39,155 --> 00:21:40,568
Sir!

288
00:21:40,568 --> 00:21:42,763
I have never been imprisoned my whole life!

289
00:21:42,763 --> 00:21:44,452
Sir!

290
00:21:44,452 --> 00:21:47,537
Sir, I don't like that woman!
My wife is more beautiful!

291
00:21:47,537 --> 00:21:49,236
You're so out of it. Put him inside.

292
00:21:49,236 --> 00:21:51,070
What do you mean?

293
00:21:51,070 --> 00:21:53,005
- Sir!
- Get in!

294
00:21:54,073 --> 00:21:57,142
Boss, boss. Maybe we can talk about this.

295
00:21:57,142 --> 00:21:58,911
Sir, please!

296
00:21:58,911 --> 00:22:00,585
Sir! Boss!

297
00:22:00,585 --> 00:22:03,060
Sir! Sir, please!

298
00:22:03,060 --> 00:22:04,817
Sir, let me out.

299
00:22:04,817 --> 00:22:06,285
Boss.

300
00:22:06,285 --> 00:22:08,388
He's been acting weird, Ma'am.

301
00:22:09,455 --> 00:22:12,222
I'm worried about his situation right now.

302
00:22:12,222 --> 00:22:14,023
<i>He hasn't come back yet.</i>

303
00:22:14,023 --> 00:22:16,208
<i>This one feels different.</i>

304
00:22:17,694 --> 00:22:20,327
It seems something is wrong.

305
00:22:20,327 --> 00:22:21,999
<i>I hope I'm wrong, Ma'am.</i>

306
00:22:21,999 --> 00:22:23,433
<i>You should check on him.</i>

307
00:22:23,433 --> 00:22:27,169
Make sure that he's okay.

308
00:22:40,286 --> 00:22:42,687
Kid, you can get out now.

309
00:22:56,476 --> 00:22:58,178
Liam, son.

310
00:23:04,083 --> 00:23:05,584
Mom?

311
00:23:17,030 --> 00:23:18,731
How...

312
00:23:25,672 --> 00:23:27,731
- Mom.
- Wait.

313
00:23:27,731 --> 00:23:30,534
- What's going on?
- Is this real?

314
00:23:30,534 --> 00:23:32,169
Mom? Is this real?

315
00:23:32,169 --> 00:23:34,205
Am I dreaming?

316
00:23:34,205 --> 00:23:35,606
Mom...

317
00:23:35,606 --> 00:23:39,851
Liam, what's happening to you?

318
00:23:39,851 --> 00:23:42,586
You act like we haven't seen each other
in a long time.

319
00:23:42,586 --> 00:23:44,030
Mama...

320
00:23:45,449 --> 00:23:49,311
There was never a day that
I didn't wish to be with you.

321
00:23:51,631 --> 00:23:53,265
Son...

322
00:23:54,897 --> 00:23:56,568
Why?

323
00:23:56,568 --> 00:23:58,280
What happened?

324
00:23:59,366 --> 00:24:01,288
Mom.

325
00:24:04,520 --> 00:24:07,233
- Mama...
- What happened to you, son?

326
00:24:07,233 --> 00:24:09,428
Mama, Mama...

327
00:24:09,428 --> 00:24:11,441
Liam.

328
00:24:12,467 --> 00:24:14,701
Mama.

329
00:24:29,660 --> 00:24:31,036
Why?

330
00:24:32,229 --> 00:24:37,968
My classmate told me you're sick, Mama.

331
00:24:37,968 --> 00:24:41,172
He said I might not see you anymore.

332
00:24:41,172 --> 00:24:43,880
That's not true.

333
00:24:44,970 --> 00:24:46,685
And...

334
00:24:48,134 --> 00:24:50,535
if ever I'm gone,

335
00:24:51,465 --> 00:24:54,752
I will still watch over you.

336
00:24:54,752 --> 00:25:03,428
All you have to do
is write down everything you want to say.

337
00:25:03,428 --> 00:25:07,832
That way,
I will know what's inside your heart.

338
00:25:07,832 --> 00:25:13,752
Because I will make
all your wishes come true.

339
00:25:24,716 --> 00:25:26,827
What are you talking about?

340
00:25:26,827 --> 00:25:28,987
Oh, my dear.

341
00:25:28,987 --> 00:25:30,955
Mom, I love you so much.

342
00:25:30,955 --> 00:25:32,353
I love you so much, Mom.

343
00:25:32,353 --> 00:25:35,705
So much. So much.

344
00:25:35,705 --> 00:25:38,794
I love you so much. I missed you so much.

345
00:25:38,794 --> 00:25:40,083
Liam, come on.

346
00:25:40,083 --> 00:25:44,101
You talk as if I'm going to disappear.

347
00:25:49,480 --> 00:25:52,477
Joyce... and Dex.

348
00:25:52,477 --> 00:25:54,948
I need to wake up from this dream.

349
00:25:55,747 --> 00:25:58,880
This is not real. This is not real.

350
00:25:58,880 --> 00:26:02,120
This is not real.
I need to wake up from this dream.

351
00:26:02,120 --> 00:26:04,589
- This is not real.
- Liam?

352
00:26:04,589 --> 00:26:06,291
Not real.

353
00:26:06,291 --> 00:26:07,419
Son...

354
00:26:07,419 --> 00:26:09,827
No... This is not real.

355
00:26:09,827 --> 00:26:11,626
Liam...

356
00:26:11,626 --> 00:26:13,084
Liam!

357
00:26:24,676 --> 00:26:26,885
I will wake up.

358
00:26:26,885 --> 00:26:29,447
I will wake up.
I will wake up from this nightmare!

359
00:26:29,447 --> 00:26:31,244
Joyce!

360
00:26:31,244 --> 00:26:33,247
Dex!

361
00:26:35,667 --> 00:26:37,015
Joyce...

362
00:27:07,318 --> 00:27:08,784
What the...

363
00:27:10,622 --> 00:27:12,363
Hello, love.

364
00:27:12,363 --> 00:27:14,650
How are you feeling?

365
00:27:33,478 --> 00:27:35,705
Liam, son!

366
00:28:23,661 --> 00:28:25,362
What the...

367
00:28:27,165 --> 00:28:28,966
Hello, love.

368
00:28:28,966 --> 00:28:31,268
How are you feeling?

369
00:28:32,227 --> 00:28:33,726
Who are you?

370
00:28:35,087 --> 00:28:36,546
Love?

371
00:28:42,391 --> 00:28:45,383
Doc, is it possible
that my son got disoriented

372
00:28:45,383 --> 00:28:48,893
after he got into a fight and got beaten up?

373
00:28:48,893 --> 00:28:51,122
He was so confused last night.
He did not know what was happening

374
00:28:51,122 --> 00:28:56,100
and was saying all sorts of things.
I couldn't understand.

375
00:28:56,100 --> 00:29:00,405
It's possible if he got punched rather hard.

376
00:29:00,405 --> 00:29:03,946
He suffers what we call
the "effect of concussions".

377
00:29:03,946 --> 00:29:06,903
You said he lost consciousness,

378
00:29:06,903 --> 00:29:10,674
and now, from what I can observe...

379
00:29:10,674 --> 00:29:15,084
He's dizzy
and looks like there's a loss of memory.

380
00:29:16,421 --> 00:29:18,489
Love.

381
00:29:18,489 --> 00:29:22,966
What were you thinking?
Why did you get into a fight?

382
00:29:22,966 --> 00:29:24,721
And what were you doing
in the middle of the road?

383
00:29:24,721 --> 00:29:27,990
We almost hit you.

384
00:29:29,226 --> 00:29:34,830
Your girlfriend asked
how you were doing last night.

385
00:29:36,309 --> 00:29:37,728
Girlfriend?

386
00:29:39,148 --> 00:29:42,145
Yeah, your girlfriend called.

387
00:29:42,145 --> 00:29:47,743
So I told her I would pick you up
at the police station.

388
00:29:48,411 --> 00:29:51,248
Dear, I'm sorry.

389
00:29:51,248 --> 00:29:52,937
I took your time.

390
00:29:52,937 --> 00:29:54,150
It's okay, Auntie.

391
00:29:54,150 --> 00:29:56,527
Don't worry about it. We're family.

392
00:29:56,527 --> 00:29:59,510
What's important is we had Liam
checked by a doctor.

393
00:29:59,510 --> 00:30:02,626
Doc, thank you for coming.

394
00:30:02,626 --> 00:30:04,766
Anytime, Via.

395
00:30:04,766 --> 00:30:09,733
But I guess we should bring him
to the hospital for possible tests.

396
00:30:09,733 --> 00:30:11,902
What do you think, son? Let's go?

397
00:30:11,902 --> 00:30:14,170
Let's go to the hospital first?

398
00:30:14,170 --> 00:30:15,469
Okay?

399
00:30:22,379 --> 00:30:24,492
Where's the bathroom?

400
00:30:24,492 --> 00:30:25,774
What?

401
00:30:27,719 --> 00:30:29,353
Over there, love.

402
00:30:44,734 --> 00:30:47,269
What really is happening?

403
00:30:54,760 --> 00:30:57,513
<i>If only I could erase the past...</i>

404
00:30:57,513 --> 00:31:00,364
<i>if only I could turn back time...</i>

405
00:31:06,025 --> 00:31:08,191
Is this because of the typewriter?

406
00:31:12,038 --> 00:31:15,044
Is this because of the typewriter?

407
00:31:16,833 --> 00:31:19,069
Is it true?

408
00:31:20,203 --> 00:31:21,955
Liam?

409
00:31:26,476 --> 00:31:29,446
I can't hear him. The faucet is too loud.

410
00:31:29,446 --> 00:31:33,817
If he's throwing up,
we should bring him to the hospital.

411
00:31:33,817 --> 00:31:35,119
Oh my gosh.

412
00:31:35,119 --> 00:31:37,187
Liam!

413
00:31:37,187 --> 00:31:41,392
Liam, are you throwing up?

414
00:31:56,173 --> 00:31:58,375
Liam!

415
00:31:59,209 --> 00:32:01,478
What? Why?

416
00:32:09,520 --> 00:32:11,488
- Mom...
- What?

417
00:32:11,488 --> 00:32:14,391
Do you remember your typewriter?

418
00:32:14,391 --> 00:32:15,759
What typewriter?

419
00:32:15,759 --> 00:32:18,228
It's a...

420
00:32:18,228 --> 00:32:20,531
It's with the other stuff
we left in Dad's care

421
00:32:20,531 --> 00:32:22,815
after our house burned down.

422
00:32:27,371 --> 00:32:30,608
Oh, if you're looking for our old stuff,

423
00:32:30,608 --> 00:32:32,743
I took them back from Danilo.

424
00:32:32,743 --> 00:32:35,060
They're in our stockroom.

425
00:32:35,827 --> 00:32:38,882
They're in our house?

426
00:32:38,882 --> 00:32:42,119
Even the typewriter is there?

427
00:32:42,119 --> 00:32:44,788
Then let's go. Let's check it out.

428
00:32:44,788 --> 00:32:46,323
Wait, wait.

429
00:32:46,323 --> 00:32:48,016
Where do we live?

430
00:32:49,760 --> 00:32:51,141
Liam.

431
00:32:52,396 --> 00:32:55,432
- I really don't know.
- Liam, come on, let's go.

432
00:33:12,983 --> 00:33:15,719
<i>I thought everything was just a dream</i>

433
00:33:15,719 --> 00:33:18,122
<i>and I would wake up back to reality.</i>

434
00:33:18,122 --> 00:33:19,990
<i>But this is a different reality.</i>

435
00:33:19,990 --> 00:33:22,026
<i>And who is this beautiful woman?</i>

436
00:33:22,026 --> 00:33:24,772
<i>They say she's my girlfriend.
How did it happen?</i>

437
00:33:26,973 --> 00:33:28,287
Liam.

438
00:33:29,533 --> 00:33:30,951
What?

439
00:33:33,404 --> 00:33:36,841
Via, I'll bring Liam home for now.

440
00:33:36,841 --> 00:33:38,710
- Okay, Auntie.
- Yeah.

441
00:33:38,710 --> 00:33:40,612
I'm sorry for bothering you.

442
00:33:40,612 --> 00:33:42,413
It's okay.

443
00:33:42,413 --> 00:33:43,548
Come on, let's go.

444
00:33:43,548 --> 00:33:47,264
You said you had to find something at home?

445
00:33:48,386 --> 00:33:50,355
Let's go? Come on.

446
00:33:50,355 --> 00:33:52,790
- I'll keep you updated, okay?
- Okay, Auntie.

447
00:33:52,790 --> 00:33:54,792
Let's go, Liam.

448
00:34:12,243 --> 00:34:14,290
Is this our house, Mom?

449
00:34:16,914 --> 00:34:22,167
Looks like you really got injured
from the fight.

450
00:34:25,189 --> 00:34:27,358
Yes, this is our house.

451
00:34:27,358 --> 00:34:30,234
You bought it for me.

452
00:34:31,562 --> 00:34:35,233
This was a surprise gift you gave me
when I got out of the hospital

453
00:34:35,233 --> 00:34:38,162
after I had the surgery.

454
00:34:43,413 --> 00:34:46,060
I gave you this house?

455
00:34:47,745 --> 00:34:49,355
Yes, Liam.

456
00:34:50,206 --> 00:34:52,587
I also paid for your surgery?

457
00:34:57,789 --> 00:35:00,868
Does it mean I have lots of money, Mom?

458
00:35:02,635 --> 00:35:06,664
I don't ask you how much you make, Liam.

459
00:35:06,664 --> 00:35:08,039
Yeah.

460
00:35:08,039 --> 00:35:09,801
Well... well...

461
00:35:09,801 --> 00:35:12,170
The stockroom you're talking about, Mom...

462
00:35:12,170 --> 00:35:13,805
Where is it?

463
00:35:13,805 --> 00:35:15,907
- The stockroom?
- Yes.

464
00:35:15,907 --> 00:35:17,540
Over there.

465
00:35:19,043 --> 00:35:20,516
Wait here.

466
00:35:23,314 --> 00:35:24,912
Liam?

467
00:35:41,632 --> 00:35:43,301
Liam?

468
00:35:43,301 --> 00:35:45,369
Mom, the typewriter isn't here.

469
00:35:45,369 --> 00:35:46,887
Where could it be?

470
00:35:48,172 --> 00:35:51,776
These are all the things
we were able to save.

471
00:35:51,776 --> 00:35:55,179
I didn't notice the missing typewriter.

472
00:35:55,179 --> 00:35:57,848
Mom, I need to find it.

473
00:35:59,684 --> 00:36:03,855
Liam, it doesn't work anymore.

474
00:36:03,855 --> 00:36:07,725
From what I remember, it's already old.

475
00:36:07,725 --> 00:36:09,427
Your great, great grandfather had it way back

476
00:36:09,427 --> 00:36:11,262
during the Japanese occupation.

477
00:36:11,262 --> 00:36:13,197
No one has been using it.

478
00:36:13,197 --> 00:36:15,700
We already have cellphones and computers.

479
00:36:15,700 --> 00:36:18,302
What would you need a typewriter for?

480
00:36:18,302 --> 00:36:19,337
Where is it?

481
00:36:19,337 --> 00:36:21,869
Why are you suddenly looking for it?

482
00:36:23,141 --> 00:36:24,375
I know!

483
00:36:24,375 --> 00:36:26,911
Why don't you try asking your father?

484
00:36:26,911 --> 00:36:31,916
He was the one who offered
to keep the things we salvaged.

485
00:36:31,916 --> 00:36:33,918
I'm just not sure if he kept it properly.

486
00:36:33,918 --> 00:36:36,114
Maybe he has it. I don't know.

487
00:36:37,121 --> 00:36:39,651
Mom, can you go with me there?

488
00:36:40,424 --> 00:36:42,026
Where?

489
00:36:42,026 --> 00:36:43,280
To Dad.

490
00:36:44,228 --> 00:36:46,030
Oh.

491
00:36:46,030 --> 00:36:47,165
Hard pass.

492
00:36:47,165 --> 00:36:48,599
No!

493
00:36:48,599 --> 00:36:52,603
No. I don't want to see your father.

494
00:36:52,603 --> 00:36:54,939
We might get into a fight again.

495
00:36:54,939 --> 00:36:57,942
So, no.

496
00:36:57,942 --> 00:37:00,945
You better go there alone.

497
00:37:00,945 --> 00:37:03,614
You're always there anyway.

498
00:37:03,614 --> 00:37:06,202
I'm always at his house?

499
00:37:07,819 --> 00:37:09,104
Yes.

500
00:37:10,418 --> 00:37:15,626
You do your work at his mansion

501
00:37:15,626 --> 00:37:18,586
whenever you can't finish it at the office,
don't you?

502
00:37:19,978 --> 00:37:23,202
I work at his company?

503
00:37:24,708 --> 00:37:26,393
Liam...

504
00:37:27,171 --> 00:37:30,608
Liam, maybe we need to go to the hospital.

505
00:37:30,608 --> 00:37:33,511
Looks like you have a serious case
of memory loss.

506
00:37:33,511 --> 00:37:35,517
- Let's go to the hospital first?
- Mom, hold on.

507
00:37:35,517 --> 00:37:36,681
- What?
- Wait, just wait.

508
00:37:36,681 --> 00:37:37,682
Liam!

509
00:37:37,682 --> 00:37:39,250
Liam!

510
00:37:39,250 --> 00:37:41,919
Get some rest first!

511
00:37:41,919 --> 00:37:43,674
Liam.

512
00:37:46,524 --> 00:37:49,159
Gosh, this kid.

513
00:37:55,032 --> 00:37:56,276
Dad!

514
00:37:57,134 --> 00:37:58,606
Anybody home?

515
00:38:05,109 --> 00:38:06,811
Sir Liam.

516
00:38:06,811 --> 00:38:09,113
Sir Danilo and Sir Vergil aren't home yet.

517
00:38:09,113 --> 00:38:11,169
Come in.

518
00:38:12,383 --> 00:38:13,832
Okay.

519
00:38:46,083 --> 00:38:49,653
Have you seen an antique typewriter around?

520
00:38:55,426 --> 00:38:58,950
Are you looking for
your mom's old typewriter?

521
00:39:03,034 --> 00:39:04,547
Yes, Dad.

522
00:39:05,403 --> 00:39:08,306
You should talk to your brother about that.

523
00:39:08,306 --> 00:39:12,182
Vergil turned the old stockroom
into his home office.

524
00:39:22,920 --> 00:39:28,792
Dad told me to ask you
about my mom's old typewriter.

525
00:39:30,127 --> 00:39:32,463
Are you trying to be a junk collector now?

526
00:39:32,463 --> 00:39:33,831
That's nice.

527
00:39:33,831 --> 00:39:37,435
Keep on doing that. You're doing a good job.

528
00:39:37,435 --> 00:39:39,136
I need the typewriter right now.

529
00:39:39,136 --> 00:39:41,672
I need to see it now.

530
00:39:41,672 --> 00:39:44,108
My mom told me you guys might have kept it

531
00:39:44,108 --> 00:39:46,344
after our house burned down.

532
00:39:46,344 --> 00:39:49,180
You think this is the lost-and-found?

533
00:39:49,180 --> 00:39:52,616
Your bastard child is really something, Dad.

534
00:39:52,616 --> 00:39:55,319
Stop, you two.

535
00:39:55,319 --> 00:39:59,657
You're fighting over a useless typewriter.

536
00:39:59,657 --> 00:40:02,994
If you're looking for the rusty typewriter,
it's gone.

537
00:40:02,994 --> 00:40:04,261
I threw it away.

538
00:40:04,261 --> 00:40:07,531
What? Why did you throw it away?

539
00:40:07,531 --> 00:40:09,567
Are you out of your mind?

540
00:40:09,567 --> 00:40:11,035
Didn't you say you no longer needed it

541
00:40:11,035 --> 00:40:13,104
when you and your mom retrieved your things?

542
00:40:13,104 --> 00:40:14,972
What do you expect me to do with it?

543
00:40:14,972 --> 00:40:16,707
We don't collect dust here.

544
00:40:16,707 --> 00:40:18,075
Where did you throw it?

545
00:40:18,075 --> 00:40:20,177
Is there a junk collector around?

546
00:40:20,177 --> 00:40:21,579
Or did you bring it to a junk shop?

547
00:40:21,579 --> 00:40:22,780
Liam, what's with you?

548
00:40:22,780 --> 00:40:25,182
When it's gone, it's gone.

549
00:40:25,182 --> 00:40:28,619
It's a useless typewriter.

550
00:40:28,619 --> 00:40:32,523
You barge in here
looking for that old typewriter.

551
00:40:32,523 --> 00:40:34,558
You didn't even offer an explanation.

552
00:40:34,558 --> 00:40:39,897
I waited for you in our meeting
with the new client in Casa Fuerte.

553
00:40:39,897 --> 00:40:41,632
You didn't come!

554
00:40:41,632 --> 00:40:43,567
You didn't even say a thing!

555
00:40:43,567 --> 00:40:45,636
I asked Borj where you were.

556
00:40:45,636 --> 00:40:49,206
He said you were going through something.

557
00:40:49,206 --> 00:40:50,408
Based on his look,

558
00:40:50,408 --> 00:40:52,977
he seems to be going through
something serious.

559
00:40:52,977 --> 00:40:56,580
Or rather, he was seriously hit on the face.

560
00:40:57,915 --> 00:41:01,419
If you're going through something,

561
00:41:01,419 --> 00:41:04,922
set an appointment
with the company psychiatrist.

562
00:41:04,922 --> 00:41:07,324
Get your act together!

563
00:41:07,324 --> 00:41:12,729
You better be ready for the
groundbreaking ceremony of our new project.

564
00:41:27,311 --> 00:41:31,215
<i>Joyce, Dex, I don't know where you are.</i>

565
00:41:31,215 --> 00:41:35,267
<i>I promise I'll do everything to find you.</i>

566
00:41:56,167 --> 00:42:00,934
[Joycelyn Trinidad Herrera]

567
00:42:00,934 --> 00:42:09,601
[Dexter Trinidad Herrera]

568
00:42:29,491 --> 00:42:31,127
Liam.

569
00:42:33,744 --> 00:42:35,475
Liam.

570
00:42:36,447 --> 00:42:40,468
I knew you'll come back to this place.

571
00:42:43,154 --> 00:42:52,997
Liam... You know...
I don't understand what's going on.

572
00:42:55,166 --> 00:42:57,349
I don't know.

573
00:43:00,004 --> 00:43:02,433
But I understand

574
00:43:02,434 --> 00:43:07,018
if you're still uncomfortable
opening up to me.

575
00:43:11,789 --> 00:43:14,551
Just always remember, I'm here.

576
00:43:14,552 --> 00:43:17,306
I'm always here for you, Liam.

577
00:43:22,477 --> 00:43:24,261
My son...

578
00:43:24,261 --> 00:43:25,582
Mom.

579
00:43:30,367 --> 00:43:32,271
Mom, thank you.

580
00:43:35,933 --> 00:43:38,369
Thank you for being here.

581
00:43:41,645 --> 00:43:44,315
I love you so much.

582
00:43:44,315 --> 00:43:46,056
So much.

583
00:43:47,251 --> 00:43:49,401
Liam...

584
00:44:16,547 --> 00:44:18,582
<i>Mom...</i>

585
00:44:18,582 --> 00:44:22,119
<i>I hope you don't think that I'm unhappy.</i>

586
00:44:22,119 --> 00:44:25,623
<i>I'm so happy you're alive and with me.</i>

587
00:44:25,623 --> 00:44:29,397
<i>But I know that something's missing.</i>

588
00:44:35,934 --> 00:44:41,933
[Alternate timeline / alternate reality]

589
00:44:41,934 --> 00:44:42,833
[Search more]

590
00:44:42,834 --> 00:44:46,033
[Alternate Reality Fiction]
[Comics, movies and more!]

591
00:44:46,033 --> 00:44:49,234
[The Theory of 2 Worlds]
[Best Fiction Stories]

592
00:44:50,087 --> 00:44:52,715
<i>Fictional stories.</i>

593
00:44:52,716 --> 00:44:56,654
<i>This only happens in comics or in movies.</i>

594
00:44:56,654 --> 00:44:59,411
<i>How is it happening to me?</i>

595
00:45:03,133 --> 00:45:07,667
[Antique Typewriters Philippines]

596
00:45:19,901 --> 00:45:21,533
[Magical Antique Typewriters Philippines]

597
00:45:21,534 --> 00:45:27,434
[No results found]

598
00:45:31,868 --> 00:45:37,433
[Incoming Call: Love]

599
00:45:37,434 --> 00:45:38,762
[Connecting...]

600
00:45:38,762 --> 00:45:40,030
<i>Hi, love.</i>

601
00:45:40,030 --> 00:45:40,968
<i>How are you?</i>

602
00:45:40,968 --> 00:45:44,601
- Hi.
- <i>I'm still worried about you.</i>

603
00:45:44,601 --> 00:45:45,803
I'm doing fine.

604
00:45:45,803 --> 00:45:47,471
<i>That's good to hear.</i>

605
00:45:47,471 --> 00:45:51,541
<i>That's all I wanted to know.
That's why I called.</i>

606
00:45:53,010 --> 00:45:55,145
- <i>Good night, love.</i>
- Good night.

607
00:45:55,145 --> 00:45:57,056
<i>I love you.</i>

608
00:46:37,694 --> 00:46:39,215
Via?

609
00:46:57,295 --> 00:47:00,188
Maybe I really suffered a concussion.

610
00:47:03,080 --> 00:47:07,607
I'm sorry if I was weird when I woke up.

611
00:47:08,952 --> 00:47:11,705
I can't really remember anything.

612
00:47:13,824 --> 00:47:17,600
But, we met when...

613
00:47:23,501 --> 00:47:25,120
Fine.

614
00:47:26,703 --> 00:47:32,243
I won't put anything into this,
except for your head injury.

615
00:47:34,733 --> 00:47:36,446
This is a big day for my brother.

616
00:47:36,446 --> 00:47:38,094
Groundbreaking ceremony.

617
00:47:38,094 --> 00:47:41,325
The biggest mall in Asia.

618
00:47:41,325 --> 00:47:43,470
Your life changed.

619
00:47:43,470 --> 00:47:45,558
And we were dragged into it!

620
00:47:45,558 --> 00:47:47,227
- Liam!
- To the man of the hour.

621
00:47:47,227 --> 00:47:50,416
The great and hard-working congressman.

622
00:47:50,416 --> 00:47:53,477
Where's the rest of the money
from the transaction in Magallanes?

623
00:47:53,477 --> 00:47:55,281
That's 20 million pesos.

624
00:47:55,281 --> 00:47:57,421
Do you think I forgot about it?

625
00:47:58,475 --> 00:47:59,876
You probably haven't heard,

626
00:47:59,876 --> 00:48:03,613
but Sir Liam has a degree
in Creative Writing.

627
00:48:03,613 --> 00:48:08,619
And in this world where I feel trapped,

628
00:48:08,619 --> 00:48:12,239
I'm thankful that I found you again.
